    {
      "page_title": "Designing a URL Shortener at Scale",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q50. How would you design a URL shortener API that handles millions of requests per day?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Reads dwarf writes, so design for a ==fast redirect== path: cache first, database second.",
            "Generate a short code from a counter encoded in base62, or from a hash with a collision check.",
            "Seven base62 characters give 62^7, about 3.5 trillion unique links.",
            "Return `301` for permanent links or `302` when you need click analytics.",
            "Cache hot codes in Redis, and rate-limit the create endpoint."
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "POST /v1/links",
            "{\"url\":\"https://a.com/long\"}",
            "201 {\"code\":\"aZ3x9Qk\"}",
            "GET /aZ3x9Qk",
            "302 Location: https://a.com/long"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flowchart",
          "spec": {
